From bcfe3545dfde3a9be16d4140e07c69723673e258 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Revulate <76570121+Revulate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:17:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gpui_windows): prefer hardware adapters and leave WARP
 when a GPU returns

Adapter selection took the first adapter that created a device in
EnumAdapters order and logged every adapter it tried. Device-lost
recovery during a driver reset or update could therefore land on the
software adapter (WARP) and stay there.

Hardware adapters are now tried first; a software adapter is only a
fallback and logs a warning. The chosen adapter (name, vendor and device
id, software flag) is logged once after the device is created.

While rendering on a software adapter, the VSync thread checks about once
per second whether the DXGI adapter enumeration changed and a hardware
adapter is present, and then requests the existing device recovery. A
return attempt that still lands on a software adapter backs off up to a
minute until the enumeration changes again.
---
